\f0\fs26 \cf0 The entire table turned as one and saw a tall blonde standing directly behind Cracker, the swarm of dancing bodies impolitely, but rhythmically, bumping her lightly. She looked over Cracker\'92s shoulder, directly into his eyes, faces only a few centimeters apart. \'93Hey, steam-boy. I\'92ve been looking for you.\'94 Sarah glided gracefully into a chair and smiled, genuinely it seemed, at Cracker.\
Cracker was completely dumbfounded. It was Sarah, she was seeking out his company on the same day his hand-brake had bailed. These sorts of things only happened in contrived vids. Now was his chance, all he had to do was not make a fool of himself. A tall order he silently admitted. When it came to women, it was only occasionally that he managed not to stick his foot in his mouth and even when he did have the odd victory, they quickly dropped off the map, never to return his calls. The uncomfortable silence at the table was becoming, well, uncomfortable. 
\f1\i Think of something Cracker. Quickly. 
\f0\i0 He thought excruciatingly slowly as beads of sweat rapidly formed rivulets across his brow, coursing a torrent down his temples.\
\'93Nice conversation, boys.\'94 Sarah decided to break the stalemate, the turning to Halo she stared him down, \'93Love is a defence mechanism created by women to alleviate the guilt produced when they wake up with people like you.\'94\
Halo chuckled quietly. \'93You\'92re a thinker aren\'92t you? Please forgive my crudeness.\'94 
